# Timestamped copies left by install.sh and by anyone editing a live file.
# Recoverable from history by definition, and untracked they hide the one thing
# `git status` is for — a change nobody meant to make.
*.bak.*

# Paths that belong to this machine, read by release.sh — a mirror of the skill
# that install.sh does not write to. Never in a public repository.
.release.local

# Findings from a cold review — `review-YYYY-MM-DD-<object>.md`, written by this
# skill. A work order for whoever fixes the items, true on its date and
# meaningless after they land; what it produced belongs in CHANGELOG.md and in
# the notes, which is where a reader looks.
review-*.md

# Session memory written by the assistant tooling. Local, and none of a
# public repository's business.
.memsearch/
